    "narrative": "Facing Misiorowski today, the Austin Waves offense faces a significant hurdle, as the opposing starter\u2019s 2.35 xERA dictates a defensive posture for our daily cap management. **Kyle Tucker** occupies our primary outfield slot, carrying a 47.89 score that reflects his high floor despite the stifling matchup. While his position in the eight-hole suppresses his ceiling, his inherent talent remains our best avenue for production in a difficult park environment. Similarly, **Andy Pages** earns the UTIL spot with a 43.07 score; although his matchup against a high-tier arm like Misiorowski is daunting, the absence of a superior option forces his inclusion to keep our offensive output from bottoming out entirely.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involved **Luis Lara**, who finished just shy of the 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" at 33.85. While his switch-hitting profile usually offers tactical utility, the combination of facing a dominant arm in Skubal and an unfavorable batting order position effectively neutralized his upside, making him an easy bench candidate to preserve our precious game caps. We are also monitoring the rest of the roster\u2014including **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Liam Hicks**\u2014most of whom remain sidelined today due to the team off-day. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** also off, and **Luis Robert Jr.** continuing to languish on the IL, we are forced to treat today as a high-risk preservation day.",
